{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And I will harden.</b> In the first five plagues it is not written 'HaShem hardened' but 'Pharaoh's heart was hardened.' What is written in the plague of hail — 'Pharaoh's heart was hardened' — even though it is among the last five plagues, is because it is written after it 'כי אני הכבדתי את לבו,' that is to say: I have already hardened it in the plague of hail, so it is as though it were written of him 'HaShem hardened Pharaoh's heart.' And the reason is as he explained: since he did not humble himself in the first five, the Holy One, blessed be He, hardened his spirit and heart in the last five; and had Pharaoh sent Israel off then, the Holy One, blessed be He, would not have accepted it until He showed His mighty deeds."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:25.768678092Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}